  "fact_notes": [
    "オリジナル教材。架空の人物・出来事による例であり、実在の調査や実証結果ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Two schools in different countries planned an online exhibition about traditional games.",
          "ja": "異なる国の二校は伝統遊びについてのオンライン展示を計画した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Each team wanted to introduce an activity that was familiar to its own students.",
          "ja": "各班は自校生徒に身近な活動を紹介したかった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They decided to prepare posters with photographs and short explanations.",
          "ja": "写真と短い説明のポスターを用意すると決めた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "At first, the students assumed that clear photographs would be enough to explain the rules.",
          "ja": "当初、生徒は明確な写真が規則説明に十分と想定した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "One poster showed a group standing in a circle.",
          "ja": "一枚のポスターは円になって立つ集団を示した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A student at the partner school could recognize the objects in the picture but could not understand the purpose of the game.",
          "ja": "相手校の生徒は写真の物を認識できたが遊びの目的を理解できなかった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "He asked whether players were supposed to cooperate or compete against one another.",
          "ja": "参加者は協力するのか互いに競争するのか尋ねた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The creators realized that their explanation depended on knowledge that they had shared since childhood.",
          "ja": "制作者は説明が幼少期から共有した知識に依存していると気づいた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "The teams exchanged questions before revising their posters.",
          "ja": "班はポスターを修正する前に質問を交換した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They added a description of how each game began and what counted as a successful result.",
          "ja": "各遊びの始まりと成功と見なすものの説明を追加した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They also explained when special objects were necessary and how ordinary materials could be substituted.",
          "ja": "特別な物が必要な場合と普通の材料でどう代用できるかも説明した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Instead of removing every unfamiliar detail, they made the information easier for international readers to follow.",
          "ja": "未知の詳細を全て取り除かず国際的読者が情報を追いやすくした。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "During the exhibition, students noticed similarities between games that had previously seemed completely unrelated.",
          "ja": "展示中、生徒は以前完全に無関係に見えた遊びの類似性に気づいた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They discussed differences without assuming that one set of rules was superior to another.",
          "ja": "一方の規則が他方より優れると想定せず違いを議論した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The project gave them a reason to explain practices they had rarely questioned in their own communities.",
          "ja": "活動は自分の地域でめったに疑問に思わなかった慣行を説明する理由を与えた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It also showed them how an apparently simple question could reveal a hidden assumption.",
          "ja": "一見単純な質問が隠れた前提を明らかにすることも示した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "International communication requires more than translating familiar words into another language.",
          "ja": "国際的意思疎通には身近な語を別言語に訳す以上のことが必要だ。"
        },
        {
          "en": "People must sometimes explain the background that makes those words meaningful.",
          "ja": "時に語を意味あるものにする背景を説明しなければならない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The posters became more useful because their creators listened carefully to the readers' questions.",
          "ja": "制作者が読者の質問をよく聞いたのでポスターはより有用になった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A successful explanation begins with curiosity about what another person needs to know.",
          "ja": "成功する説明は他者が何を知る必要があるかへの好奇心から始まる。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
